WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.979 --> 00:00:05.090
Kate Beckinsale is no stranger to kicking
butt and taking names.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:10.699
Now, she's back with her most electrifying
performance to date in Amazon's "Jolt."

00:00:10.699 --> 00:00:14.500
We have everything you need to know about
the "Jolt" ending right here.

00:00:15.819 --> 00:00:18.920
Justin seems like the perfect guy when he's
first introduced.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.310
He's charming, but he enjoys a good dirty
joke.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:26.800
It appears as though he was specially tailored
to Lindy, and as it turns out, he was.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.539
But right at the climax of her rampage against
Gareth Fizel, he's killed by someone else

00:00:31.539 --> 00:00:33.739
before she can achieve her revenge.

00:00:33.739 --> 00:00:38.620
It seems anticlimactic, but that's when we
get the big reveal that Justin is alive.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:42.899
Not only is he still kicking around, but he
masterminded the entire operation.

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:47.309
It turns out he works for the government,
which wanted to kill Fizel but knew he was

00:00:47.309 --> 00:00:50.190
too powerful to take out via the CIA.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.019
That's where Lindy comes into play.

00:00:52.019 --> 00:00:55.590
"Even the government isn't dumb enough to
go after Fizel.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.390
Are you really that stupid?"

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.469
"You know what?

00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:00.989
I think I am exactly that stupid."

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:05.800
The government couldn't kill Fizel, but some
woman with a revenge streak became the perfect

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:06.980
alibi.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:10.650
Justin led Lindy right where he wanted her
to go, and she played her part perfectly.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:15.590
One could say the entire operation was all
for the greater good, but all Lindy feels

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.840
is betrayal.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:21.450
Justin may have the button to elicit electrical
shocks to Lindy, but it doesn't do much good

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:25.800
when Lindy overpowers her treatment, and as
expected, kills her former lover.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:31.220
Naturally, Lindy's angry after she finds out
Justin got all the information on her from

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.670
Dr. Ivan Munchin, who developed the treatment
in the first place.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:37.040
She visits him, and he's promptly arrested.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.540
Before that, he mentions how they can move
onto the next stage, and it's not until the

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:45.640
end of the film where we get a better idea
of what that stage entails.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:50.640
In a scene reminiscent of Nick Fury telling
Tony Stark about the "Avengers Initiative,"

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:54.570
a woman played by Susan Sarandon enters Lindy's
charred apartment.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:58.810
Through clever editing, we realize that she's
someone who has a past with Lindy and was

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:03.440
there when she was just a child undergoing
experiments for her abnormal condition.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:08.690
Now, it appears she wants to recruit Lindy
as part of some covert mission where her abilities

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.799
can be put to "good" use.

00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:14.720
She doesn't say who she works for and what
kinds of missions Lindy would go on.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:19.140
But chances are that said missions would likely
include killing scores of people.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:24.230
“Through our work, you'll learn to harness
your rage and target the right people.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:28.634
Humans are the most powerful, undetectable
weapon."

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.739
Susan Sarandon's cameo is the final scene
in the movie.

00:02:32.739 --> 00:02:36.870
Given everything that transpires, you might
assume that reveal is the end of everything.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:40.920
But you may want to stick around for a bit
longer once the credits start to roll.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:44.700
The bonus scene doesn't have anything to do
with the plot, but it's a nice payoff to what

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.610
we saw earlier in the film.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:50.640
When Lindy's trying to get more information
on her date's killer, she heads to a tech

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.930
shop to get more data from Justin's phone.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:57.379
While she encounters a bunch of men on the
main floor, they take her to the back containing

00:02:57.379 --> 00:03:02.290
their savviest programmer, who looks like
a hacker straight out of a '90s movie.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:06.659
She's able to give Lindy the information she
needs, and as payment, Lindy hands over the

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:10.900
keys to her car, which just so happens to
be a McLaren Spider.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:15.609
Naturally, the hacker is stoked on the new
ride in the mid-credits scene, and hopefully,

00:03:15.609 --> 00:03:19.659
she has the chance to drive it around for
a bit before the police confiscate it for

00:03:19.659 --> 00:03:22.439
its role in a high-speed pursuit earlier in
the film.

00:03:23.689 --> 00:03:28.510
"Jolt" follows in a current trend of female-led
action movies all about the kind of agency

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.590
society allows women to have.

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:34.989
From the beginning of the film, we see how
much Lindy suffers due to her condition.

00:03:34.989 --> 00:03:39.420
Rather than help her, Dr. Munchin is only
interested in testing the boundaries of how

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.299
intense her rage can get.

00:03:41.299 --> 00:03:46.280
For this reason, he tells Justin about her,
which results in all of the mayhem that transpires

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.349
in the film.

00:03:47.349 --> 00:03:51.159
Rather than attempt to recruit her, Justin
decides to manipulate her.

00:03:51.159 --> 00:03:55.590
He terrorizes her emotions and makes her believe
the one person on the planet who understood

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.180
her was taken away.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:01.900
Men control every aspect of her being, but
she regains a tiny sliver of it by the end

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:02.900
of the film.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:07.329
Susan Sarandon's character appears to offer
her another route, but it's unclear how much

00:04:07.329 --> 00:04:10.790
control Lindy will have in her life moving
forward.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:15.239
Similar themes have come up with other action
films within the last few years, like "Captain

00:04:15.239 --> 00:04:16.889
Marvel" and "Black Widow."

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:21.340
All three stories have to deal with women
forcing themselves to break free of the confines

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:23.720
placed on them from the patriarchy.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:28.110
The trend likely started in response to the
#MeToo movement, and hopefully, it brings

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:31.850
about plenty of other projects with exceptional
female characters.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:37.470
It certainly seems like the creative team
behind "Jolt" have hopes for "Jolt 2."

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:42.320
Susan Sarandon's character coming at the end
of the film hints at a whole world lying beneath

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:47.320
the surface of what Lindy knows, and another
adventure could very well be in store for

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.320
her.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:51.890
It all comes down to whether Amazon wants
to go around for another ride.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:55.760
"Jolt" just came out, so it's still a bit
early to tell if a sequel announcement is

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:56.820
in store.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:05:02.000
Star Kate Beckinsale is certainly no stranger
to leading franchises with her turn as Selene

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.390
in the "Underworld" movies.

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:08.960
"Jolt" isn't based on any pre-existing intellectual
property, so it could be her version of "John

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:13.380
Wick," launching her into a killer role she
gets to play for years to come.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:17.920
Regardless of the status of a possible "Jolt
2," fans can look forward to seeing Beckinsale

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.450
next in "El Tonto," written and directed by
Charlie Day.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:25.840
The comedy should make for a decidedly different
pace than "Jolt."

